==Irish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ga|sga|cen|t=besides; without}},<ref>{{R:DIL|8581|head=cen}}</ref> from {{inh|ga|cel-pro|*kina|t=on this side of}}; compare {{cog|wlm|amgen|am-'''gen'''|t=otherwise}}, {{cog|br|ken|t=otherwise}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ga|/ɡən̪ˠ/|/ɡənˠ/|ref2={{R:ga:Finck|II|127}}<<name:"Finck II.127">> !!! {{R:ga:Quiggin|138|428}}}}
* {{IPA|ga|q=also|a=Munster|/ɡɑn̪ˠ/|ref={{R:ga:SjPh|21|section=38}}}}
* {{IPA|ga|q=also|a=Aran|/ɡɑn/|/ɡɔn/|ref2=<<name:"Finck II.127">>}}

===Preposition===
{{ga-prep|n|l-}}

# [[without]]
# [[not]] {{qualifier|in conjunction with a verbal noun}}

====Usage notes====
* In standard written Irish, triggers {{ga-mut-link|l}} (except of ''d'', ''s'', ''t'') of unmodified nouns, e.g. {{m|ga|gan [[pingin|phingin]]|t=without a penny}}. Does not trigger lenition of modified nouns, e.g. {{m|ga|gan pingin ina [[póca|phóca]]|t=without a penny in his pocket}}. In the meaning ‘not’, does not trigger lenition of either a verbal noun or on the direct object of the verbal noun, e.g. {{m|ga|gan [[ceannaigh|ceannach]]|t=not to buy}}, {{m|ga|gan [[pingin]] a shaothrú|t=not to earn a penny}}.
* Unlike most prepositions, {{m|ga||gan}} takes the nominative case of nouns, as shown by the lack of mutation of consonant-initial masculine singular nouns after the definite article, for example {{m|ga||gan an plúr|t=without the flour}}, and the presence of ''t''-prothesis of vowel-initial masculine singular nouns after the article, for example {{m|ga||gan an t-airgead|t=without the money}}.
* Unlike most prepositions, {{m|ga||gan}} does not form prepositional pronouns, but is instead followed by the disjunctive form of a personal pronoun, for example {{m|ga||gan mé|t=without me}}, {{m|ga||gan sinn|t=without us}}, {{m|ga||gan é|t=without him}}.

====Quotations====
* {{RQ:ga:Finck|II|127|text=''ȷ imə šē leš '''gon''' ēn ńī ēkāl.'' |norm=D’imigh sé leis '''gan''' aon ní a fheiceáil. |t=He left '''without''' seeing anything.}}
* {{RQ:ga:Finck|II|127|text=''l̄aurofŭī n̥ ʒēlǵə fōs əŕ fȧ nə ciŕə, ʒā mĭøx '''gn̥''' n̄āŕə ə ve orī fuhə.'' |norm=Labhrófaí an Ghaeilge fós ar feadh na tíre dhá mbeadh '''gan''' náire a bheith oraibh fúithi. |t=Irish would still be spoken in the whole country if you {{g|p}} were '''not''' ashamed of it.}}
* {{RQ:ga:Finck|II|128|text=''hāniǵ šē ʒā rā, n̄ax mĭai šə sə mŭȧlə ən̄óxt agəs '''gon''' kūrm̥ ə ʒlakə fȳ.'' |norm=Tháinig sé dhá rá nach mbeidh sé sa mbaile anocht agus '''gan''' cúram a ghlacadh faoi. |t=He came to say he won’t be home tonight and '''not''' to worry about him.}}

